# nfs (userspace NFS-client VFS server, #153) is intentionally NOT a default
# component: it #includes <nfsc/libnfs.h> and links -lnfs, both supplied by the
# libnfs PORT, which the build builds AFTER core (build.sh order: core -> ports
# -> project). Listing nfs here made the core filesystems build require a
# not-yet-built port, so a clean/cold-sysroot core build failed (masked on a
# warm sysroot that still held a stale libnfs.a/header). Only the nfsroot
# variant needs the nfs server, so it is built in the project stage instead —
# see the aarch64a72-generic-rpi4b project's b_build_project, which runs
# `make -C phoenix-rtos-filesystems nfs nfs-install` after ports for that
# variant. The `nfs` target still exists here (defined by nfs/Makefile via the
# ALL_MAKES glob), so that post-ports build resolves it.
DEFAULT_COMPONENTS := dummyfs libext2 libjffs2
